=w.route_id and w.opened_at_ms>=ra.effective_from_ms and w.opened_at_ms<ra.effective_to_ms) pid, (select count(*) from route_assignments ra where ra.route_id=w.route_id and w.opened_at_ms>=ra.effective_from_ms and w.opened_at_ms<ra.effective_to_ms) nmatch from w) select s.service_code, count(*) operations, sum(t.n_att) attempts, sum(t.n_fail) failed_attempts, sum(t.final_ok=0) terminal_failures, sum(t.n_att>1) retried_operations, round(100.0*sum(t.final_ok=0)/count(*),4) terminal_failure_pct, count(distinct p.pid) physical_pools, sum(p.nmatch<>1) bad_match, group_concat(distinct p.pid) pools from term t join service_routes r on r.route_id=t.route_id join services s on s.service_id=r.service_id join pools p on p.operation_id=t.operation_id group by s.service_code union all select 'TOTAL', count(*), sum(t.n_att), sum(t.n_fail), sum(t.final_ok=0), sum(t.n_att>1), round(100.0*sum(t.final_ok=0)/count(*),4), count(distinct p.pid), sum(p.nmatch<>1), group_concat(distinct p.pid) from term t join pools p on p.operation_id=t.operation_id;"],"caveats":["Window is 2026-05-01 10:00 to 11:00 UTC (epoch ms 1777629600000 inclusive to 1777633200000 exclusive), selected by logical_operations.opened_at_ms; attempts are counted for those operations regardless of when the attempts completed.","Attempts and terminal failures are not interchangeable: 700 failed attempts map to only 100 terminal failures because an operation can fail on early attempts and still succeed on a later attempt (not terminal), and one operation can contribute several failed attempts. Terminal failure is defined on the final attempt only.","Retried operations (500) include operations that ultimately succeeded after retries as well as terminal failures; they are not extra requests.","Terminal-failure percentage uses logical operations (4000) as denominator (100/4000 = 2.5%); no attempt-level percentage is reported.","Physical pools are attributed by routing-time assignment effective at operation open (feed_registry